    <!-- Issue #332: org.apache.httpcomponents:httpcore / httpcore-nio 4.4.16 (CVE-2026-54399,
         CVE-2026-54428) — CONFIRMED FALSE POSITIVE, verified directly against the NVD detail
         pages on 2026-07-09. Both CVEs affect Apache HttpComponents Core **5.x** ("5.4.2 and
         earlier, 5.5-beta1 and earlier") — CVE-2026-54399 is an HTTP/1.1 message-parser resource
         exhaustion, CVE-2026-54428 is an HTTP/2 HPACK decoder resource exhaustion. This project
         uses the legacy **4.x** branch (org.apache.httpcomponents:httpcore/httpcore-nio, a
         different, older artifact lineage from org.apache.httpcomponents.core5:httpcore5) —
         4.x has no HTTP/2 support at all, so CVE-2026-54428's vulnerable code path doesn't even
         exist in what we ship. This also has no patched version regardless: 4.4.16 is the last
         release in the whole legacy 4.x branch (confirmed against Maven Central metadata).
         Present via two paths: rest-assured 5.5.7 (test scope) -> httpclient 4.5.13 ->
         httpcore, and elasticsearch-rest-client 8.19.18 (compile scope, production) ->
         httpcore/httpcore-nio directly — both resolve to the same misidentified 5.x CVE.
         Originally suppressed here on weaker "test-scope only, no patch available" grounds
         before the elasticsearch-rest-client compile-scope path was discovered; rewritten with
         the actual NVD-verified 5.x/4.x generation mismatch, which applies regardless of scope. -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>Confirmed false positive, verified against NVD directly — both CVEs affect Apache
        HttpComponents Core 5.x (different artifact lineage, groupId
        org.apache.httpcomponents.core5); we use the legacy 4.x branch
        (org.apache.httpcomponents), which has no HTTP/2 support at all (CVE-2026-54428's
        vulnerable code path doesn't exist in 4.x). See issue #332.</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.httpcomponents/httpcore.*@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-54399</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-54428</cve>
    </suppress>

